From 00f807d83ef6cf0a12688682346863c47df8ac93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban): gate remote_notices, notices and guarantee on
 the inputs the hub really changes

The landed #3439 gates never skipped on the hub (host_pass 2.131% of a core, 0 skips for
remote_notices/notices/card_change). Diagnosed read-only on the live hub: every probe returned pending
Inputs() by an early fallback, never a key mismatch.

- notices: an in-flight claim held by a LIVE process, younger than NOTIFY_CLAIM_STALE_S, with nothing of the
  notified kinds past its cursor is held, not pending (the sweep returns before delivering; recovery is
  re-evaluated by every probe via _recovery_due, so a dead holder / aged claim / new event runs the pass).
- remote_notices: a ledger claim held by ANOTHER live process is skipped by every sweep path; it no longer
  forces the pass. Own claims and dead holders stay hot. Unsettled links to archived/moved chats (the
  sweep returns before touching them) are parked, re-read per probe, so they stop holding the pass hot and
  cold. The quiet proof is published unless the replica was replaced or a task row the sweep can act on was
  written during the cold read (the raw commit stamp lost that race every time on a replica that commits
  several rows a second).
- guarantee: last_active enters the key only as its lookback verdict, and an unclaimed notice still inside
  GRACE_S is a clock (due = timestamp + GRACE_S), not work.

RED tests reproduce the hub's always-hot shapes on origin/main. No notice/wake/unlink outcome changes: every
probe still returns pending for own claims, dead holders, aged claims, undelivered events, unarchived chats.
